{#- The research group, from content/people.yml. The same list renders the CV's
    "Advisees and placement" section, so a student cannot be current here and
    finished there, as one was.

    The large commented-out "Current research group" card block that used to sit
    here has not been carried over. It was dead markup -- HTML comments still
    ship to every reader -- and every person in it is in people.yml, so nothing
    it said is lost. It is in git history if it is ever wanted back. #}
{%- set current_students = people.people | selectattr('status', 'equalto', 'current')
      | selectattr('dissertation', 'defined') | list %}
{%- set assistants = people.people | selectattr('status', 'equalto', 'current')
      | rejectattr('dissertation', 'defined') | list %}
{%- set alumni = people.people | selectattr('status', 'equalto', 'alumni') | list %}
              I'm lucky to work with and learn from a range of graduate and undergraduate students and staff researchers based at UCLA and elsewhere. I'm proud of my record of placing these researchers in Ph.D. programs, jobs in industry and civil society, postdocs, and tenure-track positions.
              <h1 class="my-4">Current dissertation students</h1>
              <div class="table-responsive-sm">
                <table class="table align-middle table-striped">
                  <thead class="border-top">
                    <tr>
                      <th scope="col"></th>
                      <th scope="col" class="text-nowrap"></th>
                      <th scope="col" class="text-nowrap">Area of specialty</th>
                      <th scope="col">Dissertation title</th>
                    </tr>
                  </thead>
                  <tbody>
{% for person in current_students %}
                    <tr>
                      <td><img src="{{ person.img }}" height=50px loading="lazy"></td>
                      <td class="text-nowrap"><a href="{{ person.url }}">{{ person.name }}</a>{% for role in person.roles %}{% if people.roles[role].get('marker') %} ({{ people.roles[role].marker }}){% endif %}{% endfor %}</td>
                      <td class="text-nowrap">{{ person.area }}</td>
                      <td>{{ person.dissertation }}</td>
                    </tr>
{% endfor %}
                  </tbody>
                </table>
              </div>
{% if assistants %}
              <h1 class="my-4 pt-3">Current research assistants</h1>
              <p>{% for person in assistants %}{% if person.get('url') %}<a href="{{ person.url }}">{{ person.name }}</a>{% else %}{{ person.name }}{% endif %}{{ ", " if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}</p>
{% endif %}
              <h1 class="my-4 pt-3">Alumni</h1>
              <div class="table-responsive-sm">
                <table class="table align-middle table-striped">
                  <thead class="border-top">
                    <tr>
                      <th scope="col"></th>
                      <th scope="col"></th>
                      <th scope="col">Role</th>
                      <th scope="col">Placement (next position)</th>
                    </tr>
                  </thead>
                  <tbody>
{% for person in alumni %}
                    <tr>
                      <td>{% if person.get('img') %}<img src="{{ person.img }}" height=50px loading="lazy">{% endif %}</td>
                      <td>{% if person.get('url') %}<a href="{{ person.url }}">{{ person.name }}</a>{% else %}{{ person.name }}{% endif %}</td>
{#- Two roles read as one phrase: "Dissertation committee; graduate student
    researcher". Only the first is capitalized, so the second uses the CV's
    lowercase wording rather than a second sentence-initial capital. #}
                      <td>{% for role in person.roles %}{{ people.roles[role].site if loop.first else people.roles[role].cv }}{{ "; " if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}</td>
                      <td>{{ person.get('placement', '') }}</td>
                    </tr>
{% endfor %}
                  </tbody>
                </table>
              </div>
